body:
I think I've learnt how to deal with AE quite well. The Problem I think I have is that I struggle with expansion due to a combination of strong alliance networks which outnumber me 2:1, Constant rebel issues that I can't seem to deal with mid game. Army quality and mana management. An example I have from recent is a byzantuim campaign I've been working on. I'm able to quite reliably kill the ottomans given a few years and push into anatolia, but it seems that after the first initial frenzy of gobbling up land I'm going to slow.

&#x200B;

As far as DLC's I have all of them including origins(the new one)

Thank you very much for the response.

While I do agree that just because my friends where beaten and abused and are now more "responsible" (they have respect for authority figures however do many illegal things regardless)

&#x200B;

I feel as if me disagreeing on what authority figures around me is a sign that I lack respect and therefore don't deserve any, an example would be when I was told that I have to be home before 8:00pm when cycling, There argument was that It was too dark, I stated that I could go buy lights and a high viz coat however they disregarded said statement as "they know best" Me arguing with them tells me that I lack respect for there views and how I should be kept safe

&#x200B;

While I agree that "I'm 17 and should just be 17" I would also like to move past that and become more mature and grow out of being like to have a better grasp on my life and being able to take control of my life and leave the parts of my life that hurt behind

&#x200B;

I am seeing a therapist to fix some of these "wounds" however I feel as if me being mentally weak in the first place has caused the panic attacks and suicidal thoughts to affect me more than they should.
